1
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:10,690
Ravi puts 2,000 dollars in a savings account.

2
00:00:10,740 --> 00:00:15,060
It pays 4 percent interest each year, added to the account.

3
00:00:15,110 --> 00:00:19,170
Next year, interest is paid on the interest too.

4
00:00:19,220 --> 00:00:23,160
After 3 years, has his money grown by exactly 12 percent?

5
00:00:23,210 --> 00:00:26,450
Pause the video and choose.

6
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:26,670
No.

7
00:00:26,720 --> 00:00:29,810
Each year's 4 percent is of a bigger amount.

8
00:00:29,860 --> 00:00:33,930
So the total growth is a bit more than 12 percent.

9
00:00:33,980 --> 00:00:38,360
Remember: to increase by 20 percent, multiply by 1.2.

10
00:00:38,410 --> 00:00:42,500
To decrease by 20 percent, multiply by 0.8.

11
00:00:42,550 --> 00:00:49,800
A compound percentage change applies the percentage again and again, each time to the new amount.

12
00:00:49,850 --> 00:00:53,510
After 3 years Ravi has 2,249 dollars 73.

13
00:00:53,560 --> 00:00:59,710
That is more than 2,240, which is what 12 percent would give.

14
00:00:59,760 --> 00:01:00,440
Your turn.

15
00:01:00,490 --> 00:01:03,590
Times 1.04, three times, is one multiplier.

16
00:01:03,640 --> 00:01:05,940
What is it, to 3 decimal places?

17
00:01:05,990 --> 00:01:09,320
Pause the video and try it.

18
00:01:09,370 --> 00:01:11,700
1.04 cubed is 1.124864.

19
00:01:11,750 --> 00:01:15,330
To 3 decimal places, that is 1.125.

20
00:01:15,380 --> 00:01:20,120
So the money grows by about 12.5 percent.

21
00:01:20,170 --> 00:01:24,470
Values that fall each year use a multiplier less than 1.

22
00:01:24,520 --> 00:01:32,240
A car that loses 15 percent a year keeps 85 percent: value equals start, times 0.85 to the N.

23
00:01:32,290 --> 00:01:33,800
Here is the method.

24
00:01:33,850 --> 00:01:36,100
Step 1: find the multiplier.

25
00:01:36,150 --> 00:01:42,310
1 plus R over 100 for an increase, 1 minus R over 100 for a decrease.

26
00:01:42,360 --> 00:01:46,460
Step 2: raise it to the power of the number of years.

27
00:01:46,510 --> 00:01:49,960
Step 3: multiply by the starting amount.

28
00:01:50,010 --> 00:01:52,710
Step 4: round only at the end.

29
00:01:52,760 --> 00:01:55,130
A car is worth 18,000 dollars.

30
00:01:55,180 --> 00:01:58,590
It loses 15 percent of its value each year.

31
00:01:58,640 --> 00:02:01,640
What is it worth after 2 years?

32
00:02:01,690 --> 00:02:02,380
Your turn.

33
00:02:02,430 --> 00:02:06,020
What is the multiplier for a 15 percent decrease?

34
00:02:06,070 --> 00:02:09,060
Pause and work it out.

35
00:02:09,110 --> 00:02:14,730
100 minus 15 is 85 percent, so the multiplier is 0.85.

36
00:02:14,780 --> 00:02:22,210
After 2 years: 18,000 times 0.85 squared, which is 13,005 dollars.

37
00:02:22,260 --> 00:02:25,890
1,000 dollars earns 5 percent a year.

38
00:02:25,940 --> 00:02:29,960
When does it first go over 1,200 dollars?

39
00:02:30,010 --> 00:02:32,550
1.05 cubed is about 1.158.

40
00:02:32,600 --> 00:02:35,430
1.05 to the 4 is about 1.216.

41
00:02:35,480 --> 00:02:37,970
So it takes 4 years.

42
00:02:38,020 --> 00:02:42,340
A price rises 10 percent one year, and 10 percent the next.

43
00:02:42,390 --> 00:02:44,640
Kai works out the total change.

44
00:02:44,690 --> 00:02:46,670
Which line is wrong?

45
00:02:46,720 --> 00:02:47,880
Line 1 is wrong.

46
00:02:47,930 --> 00:02:52,210
The second 10 percent is of the new, bigger price.

47
00:02:52,260 --> 00:02:54,400
1.1 times 1.1 is 1.21.

48
00:02:54,450 --> 00:02:57,930
That is a 21 percent increase.

49
00:02:57,980 --> 00:03:04,170
Banks, loans, inflation and population growth all use compound percentages.

50
00:03:04,220 --> 00:03:11,630
A town of 25,000 that grows 2 percent a year has about 27,600 people after 5 years.

51
00:03:11,680 --> 00:03:13,000
One last question.

52
00:03:13,050 --> 00:03:16,660
A price rises 10 percent, then falls 10 percent.

53
00:03:16,710 --> 00:03:19,010
What is the overall multiplier?

54
00:03:19,060 --> 00:03:22,470
Pause the video and answer.

55
00:03:22,520 --> 00:03:24,430
1.1 times 0.9 is 0.99.

56
00:03:24,480 --> 00:03:29,150
That is a 1 percent decrease overall, not zero.

57
00:03:29,200 --> 00:03:34,360
To remember: the multiplier is 1 plus or minus R over 100.

58
00:03:34,410 --> 00:03:38,230
For N years, raise the multiplier to the power N.

59
00:03:38,280 --> 00:03:41,320
Changes one after another multiply.

60
00:03:41,370 --> 00:03:43,610
Round at the end.

61
00:03:43,660 --> 00:03:48,750
Great work! Now practise lesson 3.3 on Camday.
